<h1>Introduction to Basketball</h1>

<p><strong>Basketball</strong> is a high-paced, energetic team sport played by two teams of five players each. The objective is to score points by throwing the ball through the opponent's hoop.</p>

<div class="highlight">
  <p>Basketball is a blend of speed, skill, strategy, and teamwork — and it’s one of the most widely watched sports in the world.</p>
</div>

<h2><span class="emoji">🏀</span>Basic Rules of Basketball</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A game is typically played in 4 quarters of 12 minutes each (NBA rules).</li>
  <li>The court has two hoops — one at each end — and players score by shooting the ball through the opposing team's hoop.</li>
  <li>Each basket scored inside the arc is worth 2 points, outside the arc is 3 points, and free throws are worth 1 point.</li>
  <li>Players can move the ball by dribbling (bouncing while running) or passing to teammates.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧍‍♂️</span>Player Positions</h2>
<p>Each player has a unique role on the court:</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Position</th>
    <th>Role</th>
    <th>Example</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Point Guard</strong></td>
    <td>Leads the team, handles the ball, sets up plays</td>
    <td>Stephen Curry</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Shooting Guard</strong></td>
    <td>Scores from distance, strong in offense</td>
    <td>Devin Booker</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Small Forward</strong></td>
    <td>Versatile — scores, defends, and rebounds</td>
    <td>LeBron James</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Power Forward</strong></td>
    <td>Strong in rebounds and inside scoring</td>
    <td>Giannis Antetokounmpo</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Center</strong></td>
    <td>Tallest player — blocks shots, scores close to the basket</td>
    <td>Joel Embiid</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="emoji">🏆</span>Major Basketball Leagues</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>NBA</strong> (USA) – The most popular and competitive league in the world.</li>
  <li><strong>WNBA</strong> – Women’s National Basketball Association.</li>
  <li><strong>FIBA World Cup</strong> – International competition for national teams.</li>
  <li><strong>EuroLeague</strong> – Top professional league in Europe.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">💪</span>Core Skills in Basketball</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dribbling:</strong> Moving the ball while maintaining control.</li>
  <li><strong>Shooting:</strong> Putting the ball in the hoop.</li>
  <li><strong>Passing:</strong> Moving the ball between teammates.</li>
  <li><strong>Rebounding:</strong> Grabbing the ball after a missed shot.</li>
  <li><strong>Defense:</strong> Preventing the other team from scoring.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">📋</span>Common Terms and Violations</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Term</th>
    <th>Meaning</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Traveling</strong></td>
    <td>Moving without dribbling the ball</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Double Dribble</strong></td>
    <td>Stopping and starting dribble again</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Foul</strong></td>
    <td>Illegal physical contact with an opponent</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Shot Clock</strong></td>
    <td>Time limit (usually 24 seconds) to attempt a shot</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="emoji">📊</span>Scoring Overview</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Field Goal:</strong> 2 points (inside arc) or 3 points (outside arc)</li>
  <li><strong>Free Throw:</strong> 1 point, awarded after certain fouls</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧠</span>Concept Check</h2>
<ul>
  <li>What is the role of a Point Guard?</li>
  <li>How many points is a shot made from outside the arc?</li>
  <li>What happens if a player double dribbles?</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">💡</span>Summary</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Basketball is a fast-paced, team-oriented sport with global popularity.</li>
  <li>It involves 5 players per team on the court.</li>
  <li>Skills include dribbling, passing, shooting, and defending.</li>
  <li>Understanding positions and rules helps improve gameplay and enjoyment.</li>
</ul>

<div class="highlight">
  <p>Practice Tip: Grab a ball and try basic dribbling, layups, and shooting drills to build your confidence!</p>
